            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sueb"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is very easy to make. I had cooked up dried garbanzo beans, and I found that I needed slightly more liquid than called for, but it might just have been my beans. This is also very easy to add extra ingredients to, as I did when I made it the 3rd time, when I added a clove of garlic and some jalapeno pepper. Great recipe!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "William Paxton"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My rating based upon my preparation notes here: There are different quality EVOO. I used one with robust flavor meant for salads and marinade. If EVOO meant for sautés is used then the end product is lacking in flavor. I doubled the salt and pepper in this recipe for better flavor. Companies prepare chick peas differently in the canning process. To prevent a grainy texture I brought them to a boil and simmered them 5-10 minutes before adding them to my blender. Varying amounts of water are in each can. I advise pouring the water from the pan into a Pyrex measuring cup, blend your peas and seasoning then add water back as necessary to achieve a desired texture.Following these notes may give you the optimal outcome. The texture and flavor is great.",
            "datePublished": "2019-09-12T20:02:21.010Z"
          },
          {
